{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Audit trail{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
    <h1>What was decided while this page was built</h1>
    <p>
        Everything below was recorded by <code>App\Security\AccessAuditSubscriber</code>, listening
        to the three events the component dispatches. The bundle keeps a logger of its own in debug
        mode — the profiler panel and the test assertions read that one — but it is not there in
        production, and an audit trail is.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
        {{ queries }} question(s) reached an entry point, {{ decisions|length }} decision(s) were
        settled, {{ refusals }} of them refusals.
    </p>

    <h2>Decisions</h2>
    <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Verdict</th><th>Strategy</th><th>Reason</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            {% for decision in decisions %}
                <tr>
                    <td>
                        {% if decision.nested %}<span class="muted">↳ </span>{% endif %}
                        <code>{{ decision.attribute }}</code>
                    </td>
                    <td><code>{{ decision.decision }}</code></td>
                    <td class="muted">{{ decision.strategy ?: '—' }}</td>
                    <td class="muted">{{ decision.reason ?: '—' }}</td>
                </tr>
            {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="muted">
        The indented rows are decisions a voter asked for while answering another one —
        <code>is_granted()</code> inside an expression is the usual case. The event carries that
        parentage, which is what lets the profiler draw a tree rather than a flat list.
    </p>

    <h2>Votes that said something</h2>
    <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Voter</th><th>Said</th><th>Reason</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            {% for vote in votes %}
                <tr>
                    <td><code>{{ vote.voter }}</code></td>
                    <td><code>{{ vote.decision }}</code></td>
                    <td class="muted">{{ vote.reason ?: '—' }}</td>
                </tr>
            {% else %}
                <tr><td colspan="3" class="muted">Every voter abstained.</td></tr>
            {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="muted">
        Abstentions are left out on purpose: most voters abstain on most questions, and keeping them
        would bury the trail.
    </p>
{% endblock %}
